          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a portable power station replace a UPS?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For routers, laptops and lights, often yes, because they tolerate a short switchover and the station provides hours of runtime. For a desktop computer, check the station's published switchover time. If it is longer than about 10-20 milliseconds or not stated, put a small UPS between the station and the computer to guarantee an instant changeover."
          }
        },
