          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How often should I replace a UPS battery?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Every three to five years for sealed lead-acid batteries, and sooner in hot rooms. Most units run a self-test and warn you with an alarm or indicator when the battery is weak. Replacement cartridges are available for the major models, and replacing the battery is usually much cheaper than buying a new UPS."
